    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.jump\n\n### Description\n\nVanilla vim uses `,` to repeat the last search, but backwards. This functionality hasn't been replicated in this module.\r\n\r\nI've tried workarounds like:\r\n```lua\r\nvim.keymap.set('n', ',', function() MiniJump.jump(nil, false, nil, vim.v.count1) end, { desc = 'Repeat jump (backwards)' })\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut this causes issues because it changes the cached direction of the 'jump chain'.",
