        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yes, having `,` repeat in previous direction doesn't really suit 'mini.jump' exactly for the reason you described - it changes cached direction. The idea is for users to reverse jumping direction by typing same letter in another case: if jumping with `f`, then type `F` and keep jumping with `F`.",
