        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I wish to use `mini.jump` only for the multiline `f`, `F`, `t`, `T` behavior (`opts.delay.idle_stop = 0`) and thus need `,`.\r\n> Would it be possible for the closing of this issue, and thus the exclusion of this feature, to be reconsidered?\r\n\r\n'mini.jump' is still usable for multi-line `f`/`F`/`t`/`T` with only `;` present (which is somewhat redundant). Current design of jumping in absolute direction with those four keys instead of relative direction with only `;` and `,` will stay.",
